### **2. The DropdownCaret Hover Lean Pattern**

**Location**: `/c/Users/stick/Github/dooph/ds-sb-searchbox-icon-hover-nudge-green-20261011175400/src/components/DropdownCaret/`

This is the canonical example of "expressive details" in the design system. The hover lean (nudge) is a fraction of one shape-morph step applied when hovering, timed on the motion scale.

#### **Token Definitions** (src/styles/tokens.css, lines 337-346 & 939-947)

```css
/* Hover nudge: how far a hovered shape leans toward the next stop (a
 * fraction of one step, applied to morph AND turn). The lean is timed on the
 * motion scale (`base`, `enter`) — gentle and non-overshooting, so hovering
 * never wobbles. */
--ui-shape-morph-nudge: 0.15;

/* DropdownCaret shape: 1 = the morphing shape behind the chevron, in its
 * square; 0 = a plain chevron, no shape and no frame around it. Values in
 * between interpolate size and colour; 0 and 1 are the designed settings. */
--ui-caret-shape-scale: 1; /* expression */

/* DropdownCaret hover lean (a fraction of one step, like
 * --ui-shape-morph-nudge, which it follows by default); 0 = no lean. */
--ui-caret-nudge: var(--ui-shape-morph-nudge); /* expression */
```

The **expression preset** (practical mode, lines 957-962) neutralizes both:

```css
@layer ds.expression {
  [data-ds-expression="practical"] {
    --ui-caret-shape-scale: 0;
    --ui-caret-nudge: 0;
  }
}
```

#### **CSS Rules for the Caret Lean** (src/styles/index.css, lines 1035-1041)

```css
/* Expressive detail: the hover NUDGE, read from --ui-caret-nudge (an
 * expression token, following --ui-shape-morph-nudge by default; the
 * practical preset sets it to 0). */
.ds-dropdown-caret-host:hover:not(:disabled):not([aria-disabled="true"]):not([data-disabled])
  .ds-expr-caret-nudge {
  --ds-shape-morph-nudge: var(--ui-caret-nudge);
}
```

The hover rule targets `.ds-expr-caret-nudge` (a class on the DropdownCaret root) and sets `--ds-shape-morph-nudge` to the expression token `--ui-caret-nudge`. This leans the shape toward the next stop on hover.

#### **DropdownCaret Component** (DropdownCaret.tsx)

The component applies BOTH `.ds-expr-caret-shape` and `.ds-expr-caret-nudge` classes to the root:

```typescript
export const DropdownCaret = ({ variant = DropdownCaretVariant.dropdown, className }: DropdownCaretProps) => (
  <span
    aria-hidden
    className={cn(
      "ds-dropdown-caret ds-expr-caret-shape ds-expr-caret-nudge relative inline-flex h-button shrink-0 items-center justify-center -my-px -mr-px",
      className,
    )}
  >
    <span className="ds-dropdown-caret-frame relative inline-flex items-center justify-center">
      <MorphRotationShape
        mode={MorphRotationShapeMode.embedded}
        shapes={CARET_SHAPES[variant]}
        restingAngle={0}
        className="absolute inset-0"
      />
      <ChevronDownIcon size={IconSize.rg} className="ds-dropdown-caret-chevron relative" />
    </span>
  </span>
);
```

**Key points**:
- The shape itself is a MorphRotationShape in embedded mode
- Two shapes per variant: `[closed, open]` (e.g., squircle → pixircle for dropdown, clover → eightLeafClover for typeable)
- The chevron sits on top at `rg` size (14px)
- No props drive state; the host CSS (`.ds-dropdown-caret-host`) reads `[data-state="open"]`, `:hover`, and `:disabled`

#### **How the Practical Preset Neutralizes the Lean**

The `.ds-expr-caret-shape` rule (index.css, lines 1013-1034) also handles the shape scaling. When `--ui-caret-shape-scale` is 0 (practical preset):
- The root width collapses from the button height to just the chevron + trailing inset
- The frame width and height become 0 (no visible frame)
- The chevron color interpolates from primary-foreground → secondary-foreground

Combined with `--ui-caret-nudge: 0` (practical preset), the entire "lean" effect is eliminated:
- No shape visible to lean
- No nudge applied on hover (the CSS rule still runs, but sets `--ds-shape-morph-nudge: 0`)

